## HCI PRINCIPLES (FRONT-001 v3.3 — enforce in all UI decisions)

- **Nielsen H1 (Visibility):** Status always visible; empty pipeline columns show "Capacity available" not blank
- **Nielsen H5 (Error Prevention):** CTA buttons disabled until requirements met; dropdowns for constrained inputs
- **Nielsen H7 (Efficiency):** "New Order" always in topbar; One-Tap Advance on each Kanban card
- **Nielsen H8 (Minimalism):** Progressive disclosure; role-gated complexity
- **Fitts's Law:** Primary CTA (New Order) in topbar — never right column; minimum 44px targets
- **Hick's Law:** One advance button per card; never show all transitions simultaneously
- **Miller's Law:** 4-step wizard breaks 15-field form into cognitive chunks
- **Jakob's Law:** Left sidebar, centered modals, search-on-type, toast in top-right — follow conventions
- **Shneiderman Rule 3 (Feedback):** Every action → Sonner toast within 100ms
- **Shneiderman Rule 6 (Reversal):** UndoToast for status advances; ConfirmDialog for destructive actions
- **Gestalt Similarity:** All badges share shape/padding; only color varies
- **Gestalt Continuity:** Left-to-right Kanban = left-to-right lifecycle flow
- **Gestalt Enclosure:** Card borders and column backgrounds group related data
- **WCAG 1.4.1:** Color is NEVER the sole differentiator — always pair with icon + label
- **WCAG 2.4.7:** Focus rings NEVER suppressed (`ring-2 ring-brand-blue/20`)
- **Doherty Threshold:** Visual feedback within 100ms of every action
- **Von Restorff:** Only ONE brand-blue primary button visible at a time in a workflow
- **F-Pattern:** Critical CTAs in top horizontal zone; no primary CTAs in right column

